{
  "version": 1,
  "_doc": [
    "X-1 PRECONDITION CONTRACT — plan-2026-07-26-anti-vacuity-9-unproven-gates.",
    "",
    "THE SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for gate preconditions. Read by BOTH the bash preflight",
    "(scripts/massu-gate-anti-vacuity.sh) and the vitest drift-guard",
    "(packages/core/src/__tests__/gate-precondition-declaration-drift-guard.test.ts).",
    "Two authoring sites is the drift class this plan exists to close — do not add a second.",
    "",
    "TWO SECTIONS, TWO DIFFERENT OWNERS:",
    "",
    "  vocabulary  AUTHORED BY HAND. The closed set of artifact classes the anti-vacuity job",
    "              provisions. Each entry carries a `probe` (a shell test, exit 0 = satisfied),",
    "              a `remedy` (the exact command that satisfies it — this string is what turns",
    "              'gate #6 is decoration' into 'adapters-built: NOT SATISFIED, run X'), and",
    "              `withdraw` (what the adjudicating probe moves aside to test the requirement).",
    "              An unknown `requires` value anywhere is a HARD ERROR, never an ignored one:",
    "              a closed vocabulary that silently skips what it does not recognise swallows",
    "              its own input (G3).",
    "",
    "  requires    GENERATED. Written ONLY by scripts/ops/probe-gate-requires.sh. Hand-edits",
    "              are reverted by the next probe run, exactly as gate-registry.json's exempt[]",
    "              is regenerated from exempt-reasons.json. If you believe a gate needs a",
    "              requirement, RUN THE PROBE — do not type it here.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS IS PROBED AND NOT GREPPED. §8 item 7 measured both static detectors and both",
    "fail, in opposite directions: a textual one returns 17/46/55/180 for one predicate purely",
    "by which files it opens, with recall stuck at 6 of 9 proven gates at every setting; the",
    "exact declared-path one has zero false positives and recall 2 of 9. Six of its seven",
    "misses are `self-proving` shell gates whose precondition lives in RUNTIME behaviour and",
    "is written down nowhere. 'Does running this gate's proof REQUIRE artifact X' is a property",
    "of EXECUTING the proof (G2), so the adjudicator executes it.",
    "",
    "ANTI-LAUNDERING. `requires[]` may never EXCUSE a gate. An unmet precondition is FATAL for",
    "the whole sweep (exit 2, verdict PRECONDITION MISSING) and is counted in NEITHER the",
    "`proven can-fail` tally NOR `failures`. There is no per-gate skip."
  ],
